Since `link.v1` 0.4 (F-120) the checks also read which policies list each
subject. Two hand edits under `deny`: `local`'s subject bound to `ground`
and `local` both, which `local`'s credentials over the face still match,
though one of its names is the far principal's; and a subject selected by
the face's link protocol and bound to nobody, listed in `local`'s policy,
which hands every session over the face `local`'s grants there. Each is a
finding, and each also leaves a subject that can match the far principal
with no `@zk` deny. Exit 1.

