A window for an address that owns no state behind a face is a question
nobody asked, and passing over it would leave a misspelt owner on the
core's 60 s with the check clean: exit 2, naming the listed owners.

```console
$ zenctl check face tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --enrollment ../examples/zk2/link/radio.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml --window lab/radio-a=600 --window lab/radio-b=2
? 2
Error: --window names lab/radio-b, which owns no state behind a face of this policy (link.v1 §2.11); the listed owners of state are: lab/radio-a
check face: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

A face policy its linter refuses has no plan, and no block is judged
against it: exit 2.

```console
$ zenctl check face tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 --face-policy tests/cmd/fixtures/link/radio-router.face.toml --enrollment ../examples/zk2/link/radio.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml
? 2
Error: --face-policy: the face policy is refused (link.v1 §2.1): error router_attach [face radio] attach. Router to router is refused (§8.5, §11.3: on a router-to-router link, a deny hides a denied declaration from the far side, but its key string still crosses (spike S3: 11,330 B and 201 denied keys, against 506 B and none in a south region)): attach the far router in a south region (attach = "south-region", region = "<name>"), or the far session as a client (attach = "client")
check face: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```
